[ti:My Body Made of Light]
[ar:Giuntru]
[re:Automatic line alignment - listening review pending]
[00:16.58]I feel your light move under my skin
[00:23.50]A quiet heat that pulls me in
[00:28.96]You trace my breath with fingertips
[00:32.60]A glow that rises past my lips
[00:38.30]No shadows left between our names
[00:41.60]Just warmth that changes what remains
[00:44.04]You touch the dark I used to hide
[00:46.54]And turn it soft from deep inside
[00:49.00]If every spark becomes a sign
[00:51.58]Then let your glow return to mine
[00:54.42]My body made of light
[00:59.56]A warmth that opens through the night
[01:02.02]No fear no scripts no borrowed lines
[01:04.50]Just you and I in rising shine If everything we are is fire
[01:09.54]Then let it burn a little higher My body made of light
[01:15.42]And pulled toward something brighter
[01:29.62]Your breath is heat against my frame
[01:31.92]A silver tremor through my veins
[01:34.36]You press your palm along my spine
[01:36.70]And every fault becomes divine
[01:39.14]No need for rules no need for roles
[01:41.66]Just touch rewriting all my folds
[01:44.16]You lift the dark from where I bend
[01:46.58]And teach my pulse to rise again
[01:49.06]If every glow you leave is true
[01:50.96]Then let it shine me back to you
[01:54.42]My body made of light
[01:59.06]A warmth that opens through the night
